title: The Price of Bread
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and c_prices_timer <= 0 and (year >= 1922 or inflation >= 30)
on-arrival: c_prices_timer = 4; month_actions += 1
frequency: 250
is-card: true
tags: movement

= The Price of Bread

[? if inflation < 60 : The mark is sliding. Wages are renegotiated every month, and every month they buy less. ?][? if inflation >= 60 : The mark is collapsing. Workers are paid twice a day and run to the shops before the prices change again. Farmers will not sell grain for paper. ?] In the markets, traders hold back butter and potatoes until the price rises, and the women in the queues know it.

In some towns, works councils and housewives have formed control committees to watch the prices.

- @committees: Elect control committees in every market.
- @seize: Seize the hoarded food and sell it at fair prices.
- @wages: Demand wages that rise with prices, with the unions.
- @easy_discard

@committees
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Elected committees inspect the shops and the stores. Worker support grows.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council work.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 5;
Q.militancy += 3;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 2;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Committees of workers and housewives walk the markets with notebooks. Traders caught hoarding find their names in the local party paper.

@seize
subtitle: Bread for today; police for tomorrow. The Left's line.
on-arrival: militancy += 8; repression += 6; worker_support += 4; stability -= 2; offensive_satisfaction += 6; unionist_satisfaction -= 3; lean_offensive += 2

A crowd opens a potato warehouse and sells its contents at last month's prices, paying the owner in cash. The owner calls the police anyway.

@wages
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A joint demand with the unions and the social democrats. The Right's line.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Wages tied to the cost of living: the demand is so obvious that the union leaders cannot refuse to sign it, though they would like to.
